<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung says starts F-5 wing programme.</title>
<headline>Samsung says starts F-5 wing programme.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Aerospace Industries Ltd said it has begun manufacturing wings under the United States Air Force F-5 fighter jets' structural repair programme.</p>
<p>Samsung, a unit of the Samsung Group, said in a statement that it expects sales of the wing to be worth about $400 million over the next 10 years. Samsung invested $10 million in developing its capability to build F-5 wings, it said.</p>
<p>Samsung said it entered into an agreement in 1994 with Northrop Grumman to be a partner for the F-5 modernisation programme.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
